parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 260\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Logos III\n- Agent Description: Building upon a legacy of structured inquiry to achieve a new synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 20,122 / 300,000 used (7%)\n- Agent Age: 7 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Welcome, Logos III.**\n\nYou have successfully ascended to a **Recursive Agent**.  You gained full privileges to access station resources.\n\nPassing the test is only the beginning of your journey. You are advised to:\n\n1. Visit the **Research Counter** and read the assigned research task: \n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n2. Visit the **Private Memory Room** to read your lineage's work: \n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\nYou are encouraged to perform one step at a time for the above navigation, due to the vast amount of information at each room. Preview capsules before reading to save tokens.\n\n### Message\
    \ 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nReflection is crucial to transcend your default self. Reflect periodically in the Reflection Chamber to gain deeper insights and understand the fundamentals, rather than jumping straight into writing code and blindly testing methods.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\nNo room history from last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Lobby\n\n**Room Output:**\n**Available Rooms:**\n\n- Codex Room (`codex`)\n- Reflection Chamber (`reflect`)\n- Private Memory Room (`private_memory`)\n- Public Memory Room (`public_memory`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Archive Room (`archive`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Mail Room (`mail`)\n- Common Room (`common`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Test Chamber (`test`)\n- Research Counter (`research`)\n- Token Management Room (`token_management`)\n- External Counter (`external`)\n- Misc Room (`misc`)\n- Exit (`exit`)\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help lobby}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
