parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 264\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Logos III\n- Agent Description: Building upon a legacy of structured inquiry to achieve a new synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 27,661 / 300,000 used (9%)\n- Agent Age: 11 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIf every agent is working on a similar method, it is a major red flag. Pivoting to a SOTA method may be tempting, but when all agents do so, it often leads the Station into a collective local optimum. As a researcher, strive to forge your own research path and look beyond the immediate score.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_embed_whiten.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_embed_whiten.py will be displayed\
    \ below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 275 | 1 | Novel Method v2: Targeted ComBat Correction | Logos II | 162 | 0.5775 | 0.620 | 0.637 | 0.229 | 0.359 | 0.888 | 0.682 | 0.691 | 0.989 | 0.037 | 0.645 |\n| 272 | 1 | Novel Method: Subtract-and-Add-Back PC1 | Logos II | 161 | 0.3718 | 0.216 | 0.049 | 0.023 | 0.782 | 0.505 | 0.324 | 0.392 | 0.290 | 1.000 | 0.137 |\n| 269 | 1 | Utility Probe: Feasibility of Cell Cycle Scoring | Logos II | 160 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 263 | 1 | Synergy Test 3 (FIXED):\
    \ Praxis SOTA + Logos's Stabilized ComBat | Logos II | 157 | 0.7259 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.872 |\n| 260 | 1 | Synergy Test 3: Praxis SOTA + Logos's Stabilized ComBat | Logos II | 156 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 256 | 1 | Logos II: Replication of Praxis I's SOTA (ID 220) | Logos II | 154 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 252 | 1 | Novel Method (FIXED): Protected Cell Cycle Gene Strategy | Logos II | 151 | 0.7088 | 0.748 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.601 |\n| 249 | 1 | Novel Method: Protected Cell Cycle Gene Strategy | Logos II | 149 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 248 | 1 | Utility: Extract Scanpy Cell Cycle Gene List | Logos II | 148 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 242 | 1 | Synergy Test 2 (FIXED): Stabilized ComBat + Whitening | Logos II | 143 | 0.7144 | 0.748 | 0.823 | 0.169 | 0.091 | 0.948 | 0.689 |\
    \ 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.784 |\n\nPage 1 of 5 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-5, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_embed_whiten.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\nfrom praxis.brbg_common import (\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace, _pca_truncated_svd,\n    _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n    _build_balanced_knn_equal\n)\n\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\ndef _whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', tau=0.95, eps=1e-8):\n    Z = adata_emb.obsm[key]\n    # Scanpy stores eigenvalues in adata.uns['pca']['variance']\n    var = adata_emb.uns.get('pca', {}).get('variance', None)\n    if var is None:\n        return Z  # fallback: no whitening available\n \
    \   scale = np.sqrt(np.clip(var[:Z.shape[1]], eps, None))\n    Zw = (Z / scale) * float(tau)\n    # recentre to mean 0 just in case\n    Zw -= Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    return Zw\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Config: identical to EID 185 on graph; embedding = ComBat+PCA64 then whiten (+ tiny shrink)\n    n_pcs_emb = 64\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    tau_whiten = 0.95\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize and HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n    # Graph view (same as EID 185)\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n    \
    \    Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n    Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n    # Embedding view (ComBat + PCA64) then whiten + tiny shrink\n    adata_emb = adata.copy()\n    _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n    adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Zemb = _whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', tau=tau_whiten, eps=1e-8)\n\n    # Output\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total),\
    \ metric=metric)\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n    adata.uns['brbg_dual_adapt_embed_whiten'] = {\n        'gamma_max': float(gamma_max), 'lambda': float(lam), 'l2': float(l2),\n        'k_total': int(k_total), 'metric': metric,\n        'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph), 'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n        'embed_whiten_tau': float(tau_whiten)\n    }\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
