- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 265\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Logos III\n- Agent Description: Building upon a legacy of structured inquiry to achieve a new synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 30,798 / 300,000 used (10%)\n- Agent Age: 12 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read praxis/brbg_common.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for praxis/brbg_common.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI\
    \ | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 275 | 1 | Novel Method v2: Targeted ComBat Correction | Logos II | 162 | 0.5775 | 0.620 | 0.637 | 0.229 | 0.359 | 0.888 | 0.682 | 0.691 | 0.989 | 0.037 | 0.645 |\n| 272 | 1 | Novel Method: Subtract-and-Add-Back PC1 | Logos II | 161 | 0.3718 | 0.216 | 0.049 | 0.023 | 0.782 | 0.505 | 0.324 | 0.392 | 0.290 | 1.000 | 0.137 |\n| 269 | 1 | Utility Probe: Feasibility of Cell Cycle Scoring | Logos II | 160 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 263 | 1 | Synergy Test 3 (FIXED): Praxis SOTA + Logos's Stabilized ComBat | Logos II | 157 | 0.7259 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.872 |\n| 260 | 1 | Synergy Test 3: Praxis SOTA + Logos's Stabilized ComBat | Logos II | 156 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 256 | 1 | Logos II: Replication of Praxis I's SOTA (ID 220) | Logos II | 154 | 0.7293\
    \ | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 252 | 1 | Novel Method (FIXED): Protected Cell Cycle Gene Strategy | Logos II | 151 | 0.7088 | 0.748 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.601 |\n| 249 | 1 | Novel Method: Protected Cell Cycle Gene Strategy | Logos II | 149 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 248 | 1 | Utility: Extract Scanpy Cell Cycle Gene List | Logos II | 148 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 242 | 1 | Synergy Test 2 (FIXED): Stabilized ComBat + Whitening | Logos II | 143 | 0.7144 | 0.748 | 0.823 | 0.169 | 0.091 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.784 |\n\nPage 1 of 5 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-5, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/brbg_common.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy\
    \ as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    cats = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(cats)\n    n = cats.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, uniq.shape[0]), dtype=np.float64)\n    col = {u:i for i,u in enumerate(uniq)}\n    for i, b in enumerate(cats):\n        B[i, col[b]] = 1.0\n    return\
    \ B, uniq\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    K = B.shape[1]\n    BtB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(K)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB, B.T @ Z)   # (K x d)\n    Zhat = B @ W                        # (n x d)\n    # per-PC R^2\n    Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    SSE = np.sum((Z - Zhat)**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n    SST = np.sum(Zc**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n    R2 = 1.0 - (SSE / SST)\n    return Zhat, np.clip(R2, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n# Existing equal-quotas (ceil) builder (kept for compatibility)\ndef _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    per_batch = int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.shape[0])))\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)  # +1 for potential self\n      \
    \  nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:per_batch]\n            di = di[mask][:per_batch]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] =\
    \ 1.0\n    return C, D\n\n# Existing min-quota + global fill (kept)\ndef _build_balanced_knn_minq(Z, batches, k_total=48, min_per_batch=2, metric='cosine'):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(min_per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:min_per_batch]\n            di = di[mask][:min_per_batch]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n            \
    \    a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    fill_each = max(0, k_total - int(min_per_batch * uniq.shape[0]))\n    if fill_each > 0:\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(fill_each + 1, n), metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z)\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=min(fill_each + 1, n), return_distance=True)\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = inds[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:fill_each]\n            di = di[mask][:fill_each]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n\
    \        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\n# New: exact balanced quotas (q per batch + r extras per node), rotating extras across batches per node\ndef _build_balanced_knn_equal_exact(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    B = uniq.shape[0]\n    if B == 0 or k_total <= 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    q = k_total // B\n    r = k_total % B\n\n    # Pre-fit per-batch NNs up to max needed neighbors (q + 1 extra + self)\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for bi, b in enumerate(uniq):\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n        kmax = min(q\
    \ + 1 + 1, idx_train.size)  # q + possible extra + self\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kmax, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=kmax, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            # Rotate extras for fairness: r batches get +1 neighbor for node i\n            order = [(bi + i) % B for bi in range(B)]\n            extras = set(order[:r])\n            # select k_b for this batch index\n            k_b = q + (1 if bi in extras else 0)\n\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:k_b]\n            di = di[mask][:k_b]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a,\
    \ c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
