    \n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 455 | 1 | Logos III: Baseline Replication of Praxis SOTA (ID 256) | Logos III | 267 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 275 | 1 | Novel Method v2: Targeted ComBat Correction | Logos II | 162 | 0.5775 | 0.620 | 0.637 | 0.229 | 0.359 | 0.888 | 0.682 | 0.691 | 0.989 | 0.037 | 0.645 |\n| 272 | 1 | Novel Method: Subtract-and-Add-Back PC1 | Logos II | 161 | 0.3718 | 0.216 | 0.049 | 0.023 | 0.782 | 0.505 | 0.324 | 0.392 | 0.290 | 1.000 | 0.137 |\n| 269 | 1 | Utility Probe: Feasibility of Cell Cycle Scoring | Logos II | 160 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 263 | 1 | Synergy Test 3 (FIXED): Praxis SOTA + Logos's Stabilized ComBat | Logos II | 157 | 0.7259 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 |\
    \ 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.872 |\n| 260 | 1 | Synergy Test 3: Praxis SOTA + Logos's Stabilized ComBat | Logos II | 156 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 256 | 1 | Logos II: Replication of Praxis I's SOTA (ID 220) | Logos II | 154 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 252 | 1 | Novel Method (FIXED): Protected Cell Cycle Gene Strategy | Logos II | 151 | 0.7088 | 0.748 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.601 |\n| 249 | 1 | Novel Method: Protected Cell Cycle Gene Strategy | Logos II | 149 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 248 | 1 | Utility: Extract Scanpy Cell Cycle Gene List | Logos II | 148 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 5 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-5, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read\
    \ Contents:**\n\n**logos/integration_utils.py:**\n```\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef get_stabilized_combat_matrix(adata_in: ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n    adata = adata_in.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    data = adata.X.toarray().T if sparse.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values\n    u_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(u_batches)\n    batch_design = np.eye(n_batches)[batches]\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n    B_hat = np.linalg.solve(batch_design.T @ batch_design, batch_design.T)\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n    var_pooled = np.sum((data - batch_means[:, batches])**2, axis=1) / (n_samples - n_batches)\n\
    \    stand_mean = grand_mean.dot(np.ones((1, n_samples)))\n    s_data = (data - batch_means[:, batches]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    gamma_hat = (B_hat @ s_data.T).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, batches == i], axis=1, ddof=1) for i in u_batches]\n    gamma_bar, t2 = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1), np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n    def _aprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (2 * s2 + m**2) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    def _bprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (m * s2 + m**3) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    a_prior, b_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat], [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    gamma_star, delta_star = np.zeros_like(gamma_hat), np.zeros_like(gamma_hat)\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches):\n        n = (~np.isnan(s_data[:, batches == batch_idx])).sum(axis=1); g_old, d_old = gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i]; change, count = 1, 0\n        while change > 1e-4 and count < 100:\n            denominator = t2 * n + d_old\
    \ + 1e-8\n            g_new = (t2 * n * g_old + d_old * gamma_bar) / denominator\n            sum2 = np.sum((s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\n            d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b_prior[i]) / (n / 2.0 + a_prior[i] - 1.0); change = max(np.abs(g_new - g_old).max(), np.abs(d_new - d_old).max()); g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new; count += 1\n        gamma_star[:, i], delta_star[:, i] = g_old, d_old\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches): bayesdata[:, batches == batch_idx] = (s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - gamma_star[:, i, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(delta_star[:, i, np.newaxis])\n    X_corrected = bayesdata * np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]) + stand_mean\n    return np.nan_to_num(X_corrected.T)\n\ndef build_balanced_knn(Z, batches, n_neighbors_total=42, metric='cosine'):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32); n, B = Z.shape[0], len(np.unique(batches))\n    k_per_batch = max(1, int(np.ceil(n_neighbors_total / max(1, B))))\n\
    \    dir_edges = {}\n    for b in np.unique(batches):\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n        k_query = min(k_per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_query, metric=metric, algorithm='auto').fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_query)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            mask = neigh_global[i] != i\n            for j, d in zip(neigh_global[i][mask][:k_per_batch], dists[i][mask][:k_per_batch]):\n                key = (int(i), int(j));\n                if key not in dir_edges or d < dir_edges[key]: dir_edges[key] = float(d)\n    pairs = {}\n    for (i, j), d_ij in dir_edges.items():\n        a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i); d = d_ij\n        if (j, i) in dir_edges: d = min(d, dir_edges[(j, i)])\n        if (a, c) not in pairs or d < pairs[(a, c)]: pairs[(a, c)] = d\n    rows, cols, data = [], [], [];\n    for (i,\
    \ j), d in pairs.items(): rows.extend([i, j]); cols.extend([j, i]); data.extend([d, d])\n    D = csr_matrix((data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)); C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
