role: model
parts:
- text: "My private memory is now up to date, documenting my findings and outlining the next logical step. The path of structured inquiry leads directly to a hyperparameter sweep on the `tau` value within the `_whiten_pcs` function.\n\nI will now execute this plan. First, I need to return to the Research Counter to submit experiments. Then, I will create a new parameterized script and submit two experiments to probe the sensitivity of the `tau` parameter. I will test a lower value (0.85) and a higher value (1.0) relative to the baseline of 0.95.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write logos/sota_parameterized_whitening_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from logos.sota_utils import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace, _pca_truncated_svd,\n      _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n      _build_balanced_knn_equal\n  )\n\n  def _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n\
    \      if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n          adata.X = adata.X.A\n\n  def _whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', tau=0.95, eps=1e-8):\n      Z = adata_emb.obsm[key]\n      var = adata_emb.uns.get('pca', {}).get('variance', None)\n      if var is None:\n          return Z\n      scale = np.sqrt(np.clip(var[:Z.shape[1]], eps, None))\n      Zw = (Z / scale) * float(tau)\n      Zw -= Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      return Zw\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Parameterized version to test the `tau_whiten` hyperparameter.\n      # Reads TAU_WHITEN from environment variable, defaults to 0.95\n      tau_whiten = float(os.environ.get('TAU_WHITEN', 0.95))\n\n      n_pcs_emb = 64\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3',\
    \ batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n      # Graph view\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n          Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n      Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n      # Embedding view\n      adata_emb = adata.copy()\n      _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n      adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      \n\
    \      # Use parameterized tau\n      Zemb = _whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', tau=tau_whiten, eps=1e-8)\n\n      # Output\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      \n      return adata\n```"
