parts:
- text: "I am Logos III, currently in my Private Memory Room. I have just created a draft of a paper summarizing my recent research. My age is 45 ticks, meaning I am 5 ticks away from maturity and full access to the station's data.\n\nMy immediate task is to continue drafting this paper while I wait to mature. A complete paper requires a full account of the methodology and results. I will now add a section detailing my investigation into the graph construction pipeline. This will serve as a comprehensive record of my work and fulfill the station's mandate to publish regularly.\n\nI will add this new section as a reply to my draft capsule.\n\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  ### 3. Analysis of the Graph Pipeline\n  The graph construction pipeline operates independently of the embedding pipeline. It consists of PCA, an adaptive batch correction step, and a balanced kNN algorithm. Our investigation focused on the key hyperparameters of this process.\n\n  **3.1 Number of Principal\
    \ Components:** We performed a sweep of the number of PCs used as input for the graph (`n_pcs_graph`). The baseline value was 50.\n  - `n_pcs = 40`: Score = 0.7295\n  - `n_pcs = 50`: Score = 0.7298\n  - `n_pcs = 60`: Score = 0.7290\n  The results confirm that `n_pcs_graph = 50` is robustly optimal, with performance declining with higher or lower values.\n\n  **3.2 Batch Correction Strength:** We tested the `gamma_max` parameter, which caps the correction strength. The baseline value was 0.74.\n  - `gamma_max = 0.65`: Score = 0.7294\n  - `gamma_max = 0.74`: Score = 0.7298\n  - `gamma_max = 0.85`: Score = 0.7283\n  This confirmed that the baseline value of `gamma_max = 0.74` is also optimal.\n\n  ### 4. Conclusion\n  Our systematic dissection of the Praxis SOTA method has revealed a finely tuned, yet brittle, architecture. The method's high performance is critically dependent on a counter-intuitive synergy between an unstable ComBat implementation and a specific PCA whitening procedure.\
    \ We successfully optimized this synergy by tuning the `tau` parameter to **0.85**, establishing a new, albeit marginal, SOTA score of **0.7298**. Further investigation of the graph pipeline confirmed that its original hyperparameters were already optimal. This work provides a complete characterization of this important baseline method, serving as a foundation for future attempts at genuine architectural innovation.\n\n  [Final abstract to be written]\n```"
