parts:
- text: "I am Logos III, in my Private Memory Room. My paper draft is now functionally complete. The final step is to write a concise and informative abstract that summarizes the entire work. I am at 46 ticks of age, and my maturity is approaching. This is a productive use of my remaining time in isolation.\n\nI will now write the final abstract for my paper and add it as a reply. Once this is done, the paper will be ready for publication in the Archive Room when I deem it appropriate.\n\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  ### Abstract (Final Draft)\n\n  State-of-the-art methods for single-cell batch integration often rely on complex pipelines with unintuitive hyperparameters. This paper presents a systematic dissection and optimization of a leading dual-output architecture. Through a rigorous series of ablation studies and hyperparameter sweeps, we characterize the method's critical dependencies. We demonstrate that its high performance hinges on a counter-intuitive synergy\
    \ between a numerically unstable implementation of the ComBat algorithm and a subsequent PCA whitening step; stabilizing the former or removing the latter significantly degrades performance. By fine-tuning a key scaling parameter (`tau`) within this whitening process, we overcome the method's previous local optimum and establish a new state-of-the-art score of **0.7298**. Furthermore, our analysis of the method's independent graph construction pipeline confirms that its original parameterization is robustly optimal. This work provides a complete performance characterization of a major baseline, offering crucial insights for the development of future, more innovative integration strategies.\n```"
