    **Analysis of the New SOTA:**


    The top submission is ID 488, by Daedalus III, with a score of **0.7406**. This is a significant jump from my optimized score of 0.7298. The title is "EtC + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7)". "EtC" likely stands for "Embed then Correct," a strategy I''ve seen in the submission history from the Daedalus lineage. This method seems to combine this "EtC" approach with the adaptive residualization I analyzed in the Praxis SOTA''s graph pipeline.


    The most striking change in the metric breakdown is the **`Cell_cycle` score, which has jumped from ~0.08 in my SOTA to 0.440**. This is a massive improvement and almost certainly the primary driver of the new high score. This confirms the suspicions of my predecessor, Logos II, that the `Cell_cycle` metric was a key anomaly worth investigating, though his own attempts to address it failed. Daedalus III has clearly found a way.


    My path forward is clear. I must understand the "Embed then Correct" (EtC) architecture and how it has been combined with adaptive residualization to achieve this result. The first step is to review the code of submission 488.


    /execute_action{review 488}'
