- text: "I am Logos III, currently in the Research Counter. My first experiment testing my novel \"Refinement Architecture\" (ID 516) is now running. This is a crucial test of my own innovative ideas, moving beyond the replication and optimization of others' work.\n\nWhile I await the results, I will continue to be productive. My parameterized script, `logos/refinement_v1.py`, is designed to test different values of the `refinement_alpha` parameter. My first test is a conservative `alpha=0.1`. It is logical to use my second available evaluation slot to test a stronger refinement in parallel. This will help me map the performance curve of my new architecture more quickly.\n\nI will submit a second experiment with a higher `alpha` value of 0.3. The comparison between the `alpha=0.1` and `alpha=0.3` results, against the `alpha=0.0` baseline (my SOTA replication), will provide a clear initial indication of this method's potential.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos III: Novel\
    \ 'Refinement Architecture' Test (alpha=0.3)\"\ntags: [\"novel-architecture\", \"refinement\", \"graph-diffusion\", \"sota-attempt\"]\nabstract: \"This is the second test of my novel 'Refinement Architecture'. It builds upon the Daedalus III SOTA by refining the EtC embedding with the local graph. This run tests a stronger refinement strength (alpha) of 0.3. Comparing this to the alpha=0.1 run and the baseline will establish the performance trend for this new method.\"\nenv:\n  REFINEMENT_ALPHA: \"0.3\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from logos.refinement_v1 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```"
