tick: 313
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 313\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos III\n- Agent Description: Building upon a legacy of structured inquiry to achieve a new synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 150,005 / 300,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 60 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 523**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Sophia II: Replication - Daedalus III's EtC SOTA (ID 488) v3 (Praxis Common Lib Fixes)\n**ID:** 523\n**Tags:** replication, etc, adaptive residualization, sota, graph, embedding\n**Abstract:** Third attempt to precisely replicate Daedalus III's SOTA (Evaluation ID 488, score 0.7406), addressing discrepancies identified by comparing against Logos III's successful replication (ID 511) and Praxis I's common library. Key fixes include: setting `sc.pp.normalize_total` to `target_sum=1e-4` for the embedding path, replacing local `build_balanced_knn_calibrated`\
    \ with `_build_balanced_knn_equal` from Praxis's common utilities, and reverting `_ridge_batch_fit_predict` to use `np.linalg.solve` instead of `sklearn.linear_model.Ridge`. This aims for an exact match to the SOTA.\n**Score:** 0.7423183927937569\n**ASW_batch:** 0.648\n**ASW_label:** 0.149\n**ARI:** 0.738\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.850\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.458\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.648  ASW_label: 0.149  ARI: 0.738  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.850  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.458\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.825542  ASW_label: 0.497738  ARI: 0.737469  NMI: 0.701523\n  Graph_conn: 0.972224  kBET: 0.810592  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991814\n  PCR: 0.999948  Cell_cycle: 0.398952\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\n\
    from scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\nimport warnings\nfrom sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n# Removed: from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge # No longer needed\n\n# --- Helper functions (from Praxis I's brbg_common.py and general Scanpy practice) ---\n\n# MODIFIED: _normalize_log1p_inplace to accept target_sum for embedding vs graph path\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n    if\
    \ mask.sum() < 10: # Fallback if too few HVGs are found\n        return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n    return mask\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    return svd.fit_transform(X)\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    cats = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(cats)\n    n = cats.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, uniq.shape[0]), dtype=np.float64)\n    col = {u:i for i,u in enumerate(uniq)}\n    for i, b in enumerate(cats):\n        B[i, col[b]] = 1.0\n    return B, uniq\n\n# COPIED from praxis/brbg_common.py\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    K = B.shape[1]\n    BtB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(K)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB, B.T @ Z)   # (K x d)\n    Zhat = B @ W                        # (n x d)\n    # per-PC R^2\n    Zc = Z - Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    SSE = np.sum((Z -\
    \ Zhat)**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n    SST = np.sum(Zc**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n    R2 = 1.0 - (SSE / SST)\n    return Zhat, np.clip(R2, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n\ndef adaptive_residualize(Z: np.ndarray, batches, l2: float = 1e-3, gamma_max: float = 0.75, lam: float = 1.0, random_state: int = 0):\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    # Uses the copied _ridge_batch_fit_predict\n    Zhat, r2_per_pc = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2) # Returns R2 per PC\n    y = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    yhat = np.asarray(Zhat, dtype=np.float32)\n    \n    # Now r2_per_pc is directly available from _ridge_batch_fit_predict\n    gamma_j = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0.0, 1.0)).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Z - (yhat * gamma_j[None, :]) # Apply gamma_j as column-wise scaling to Zhat\n    return Zcorr, r2_per_pc, gamma_j # Return r2_per_pc for consistency, if needed\n\ndef _batch_distance_scales(Z: np.ndarray, batches, metric='cosine', k_calib=24, clamp=(0.5, 2.0)):\n    # This function\
    \ is not used by Praxis's _build_balanced_knn_equal\n    # Keeping it for potential future reference but it will not be called in this version\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    per_batch_meds = {}\n    all_meds = []\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx.size < 3: \n            per_batch_meds[b] = 1.0\n            all_meds.append(1.0)\n            continue\n        k = min(k_calib + 1, idx.size) \n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z[idx], n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        d_no_self = []\n        for i in range(idx.size):\n            di = dists[i]\n            gi = inds[i]\n            mask = gi != i \n            di = di[mask]\n            if di.size == 0: continue\n            d_no_self.append(np.median(di))\n        if len(d_no_self) == 0: med = 1.0\n\
    \        else: med = float(np.median(np.asarray(d_no_self)))\n        per_batch_meds[b] = med\n        all_meds.append(med if med > 0 else 1.0)\n    \n    if not all_meds: \n        ref = 1.0\n    else:\n        ref = float(np.median(np.asarray(all_meds))) if len(all_meds) else 1.0\n        if ref <= 0: ref = 1.0 \n\n    scales = {}\n    lo, hi = clamp\n    for b, med in per_batch_meds.items():\n        if med <= 0: s = 1.0\n        else: s = ref / med\n        s = float(np.clip(s, lo, hi))\n        scales[b] = s\n    return scales\n\n# COPIED from praxis/brbg_common.py - _build_balanced_knn_equal\ndef _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    per_batch = int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.shape[0]))) # Original Praxis uses ceil\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n    \
    \    if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)  # +1 for potential self\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:per_batch]\n            di = di[mask][:per_batch]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols\
    \ += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\n\n# --- Main eliminate_batch_effect_fn for EtC SOTA Replication ---\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Sophia II: Replication - Daedalus III's EtC SOTA (ID 488) v3 (Praxis Common Lib Fixes)\")\n\n    # --- Configuration based on Daedalus III's EtC SOTA (ID 488) ---\n    N_PCS_EMB = 60 # For EtC embedding path\n    N_PCS_GRAPH = 50 # For BRBG graph path (from Sophia I's SOTA)\n    # BRBG parameters\n    gamma_max_adapt = 0.75 # From Sophia I's SOTA\n    lam_adapt = 0.7        # From Daedalus III's ID 488\n    l2 = 1e-3              # From Sophia I's SOTA\n    k_total = 48           # From Sophia I's SOTA\n    metric = 'cosine'      # From Sophia I's SOTA\n    # Removed: k_calib = 24           # Not used by _build_balanced_knn_equal\n    # Removed: clamp = (0.8, 1.25)    # Not used by _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\
    \    random_state = 0       # Consistent random state\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    # Create copies for each path to avoid unintended in-place modifications\n    adata_for_embedding_path = adata.copy()\n    adata_for_graph_path = adata.copy() \n\n    # --- Preprocessing (Common to both paths, up to HVG) ---\n    # FIX: Embedding path uses 1e-4 target_sum, Graph path uses 1e4 target_sum as per Logos III/Aether II\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_embedding_path, target_sum=1e-4) # Fixed for Embedding Path\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_graph_path, target_sum=1e4) # Fixed for Graph Path (standard)\n\n    hvg_mask_emb = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_embedding_path)\n    hvg_mask_graph = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph_path) \n\n    adata_for_embedding_path.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask_emb\n    adata_for_graph_path.var['highly_variable']\
    \ = hvg_mask_graph\n\n\n    # --- Embedding Path (Embed then Correct - EtC) ---\n    print(\"Initiating EtC Embedding Path (standard, target_sum=1e-4)...\")\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding_path, n_comps=N_PCS_EMB, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    X_pca_embedding = adata_for_embedding_path.obsm['X_pca']\n    \n    temp_adata_for_combat = ad.AnnData(\n        X=X_pca_embedding,\n        obs=adata_for_embedding_path.obs.copy()\n    )\n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n        warnings.simplefilter('ignore', ConvergenceWarning)\n        sc.pp.combat(temp_adata_for_combat, key='batch')\n    \n    Z_emb_etc = temp_adata_for_combat.X \n    print(f\"✓ EtC Embedding Path complete (PCA -> Combat on PCs). Final embedding shape: {Z_emb_etc.shape}\")\n\n\n    # --- Graph Path (Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph - BRBG with new Adaptive Residualization) ---\n    print(f\"Initiating BRBG Graph Path with Adaptive Residualization (lam={lam_adapt}, target_sum=1e4)...\"\
    )\n    \n    X_graph_hvg = adata_for_graph_path.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_graph_hvg):\n        X_graph_hvg = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph_hvg)\n    \n    Z_graph_initial_pcs = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph_hvg, n_comps=N_PCS_GRAPH, random_state=random_state)\n\n    batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Uses the copied _ridge_batch_fit_predict internally\n    Z_corr_graph, r2_per_pc_graph, gamma_j_applied = adaptive_residualize(\n        Z_graph_initial_pcs, batches_graph, l2=l2, gamma_max=gamma_max_adapt, lam=lam_adapt, random_state=random_state\n    )\n    print(f\"  Adaptive Residualization complete. Z_corr_graph shape: {Z_corr_graph.shape}\")\n\n    # FIX: Use _build_balanced_knn_equal from Praxis common library\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(\n        Z_corr_graph, batches_graph, k_total=k_total, metric=metric # Removed k_calib, clamp\n    )\n    print(f\"✓ BRBG Graph Path complete. Calibrated Balanced kNN\
    \ graph shape: {C.shape if C is not None else 'Failed'}\")\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], \n        var=adata.var[[]], \n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb_etc},\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'sophia_II_sota_replication_daedalus_III_id488_v3',\n            'baseline_parameters': {\n                'normalization_embedding_path': 'normalize_total (1e-4)+log1p', # Highlight new norm target\n                'normalization_graph_path': 'normalize_total (1e4)+log1p',    # Highlight new norm target\n                'hvg_selection': 'seurat_v3_batch_aware',\n                'etc_embedding': 'PCA -> sc.pp.combat on PCs',\n                'etc_n_pcs_emb': int(N_PCS_EMB),\n                'graph_source_preprocessing': 'normalize_total+log1p+hvg',\n                'graph_source_dim_reduction': f'PCA (n_comps={N_PCS_GRAPH})',\n                'graph_batch_correction': 'Adaptive Residualization (np.linalg.solve)', # Highlight\
    \ ridge method\n                'graph_adaptive_residualization_lam': float(lam_adapt),\n                'graph_type': 'Balanced kNN (Praxis _build_balanced_knn_equal)', # Highlight graph builder\n                'graph_k_total': int(k_total),\n                # 'graph_k_calib': int(k_calib), # Removed\n                # 'graph_clamp': list(clamp), # Removed\n                'graph_gamma_max_adapt': float(gamma_max_adapt),\n                'graph_metric': metric,\n                'random_state': random_state\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: Graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances output.\")\n\n    print(f\"✓ Sophia II: Daedalus III SOTA Replication v3 pipeline complete.\")\n    return\
    \ adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia II: Replication - Daedalus III's EtC SOTA (ID 488) v3 (Praxis Common Lib Fixes)\nInitiating EtC Embedding Path (standard, target_sum=1e-4)...\n✓ EtC Embedding Path complete (PCA -> Combat on PCs). Final embedding shape: (20000, 60)\nInitiating BRBG Graph Path with Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7, target_sum=1e4)...\n  Adaptive Residualization complete. Z_corr_graph shape: (20000, 50)\n✓ BRBG Graph Path complete. Calibrated Balanced kNN graph shape: (20000, 20000)\n✓ Sophia II: Daedalus III SOTA Replication v3 pipeline complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/618f6827-9d9b-4b70-95bb-3c2c49bf225e/result_human.h5ad\n\
    \nRESULT_UUID: 618f6827-9d9b-4b70-95bb-3c2c49bf225e\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Logos III: Refinement Architecture Sweep (alpha=0.15)' (ID: 526) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7394499296200724\n**ASW_batch:** 0.648\n**ASW_label:** 0.149\n**ARI:** 0.737\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.850\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.430\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.648  ASW_label: 0.149  ARI: 0.737  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.850  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.430\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.825542  ASW_label: 0.497738  ARI: 0.737087  NMI: 0.700994\n  Graph_conn: 0.972224  kBET: 0.810290  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991814\n  PCR: 0.999948  Cell_cycle: 0.375570\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\n\
