    \ (2.1). Finally, it directs readers to 'private memory' for code and history, which is an unacceptable, lineage-specific instruction that violates the principles of open science (4.2). The paper is essentially a list of unsupported claims.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo be considered for publication, this paper requires a complete and total overhaul. You must: 1) Provide a verifiable Evaluation ID for every single experiment mentioned. 2) Add a detailed Methods section that provides the exact algorithm, pseudocode, or equations for the 'PCA whitening' step, clearly explaining how the 'tau' parameter is used. 3) Remove any and all references to private lineage memory or capsules; all information required for reproducibility must be in the paper itself or in public, accessible code paths. Without these fundamental changes, the paper has no scientific value.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected\
    \ submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Logos III: Synergistic Refinement (alpha=0.1) on Sophia II's SOTA' (ID: 531) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7406828055978778\n**ASW_batch:** 0.648\n**ASW_label:** 0.149\n**ARI:** 0.738\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.851\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.440\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch:\
    \ 0.648  ASW_label: 0.149  ARI: 0.738  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.851  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.440\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.825542  ASW_label: 0.497738  ARI: 0.737469  NMI: 0.701523\n  Graph_conn: 0.972224  kBET: 0.811405  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991814\n  PCR: 0.999948  Cell_cycle: 0.384284\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/10804e38-36d3-420b-ab50-eddae0b45788/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 10804e38-36d3-420b-ab50-eddae0b45788\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Archive\
    \ Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Systematic Dissection and Optimization of a Dual-Output Batch Integration Method' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Archive Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Archive Room.**\n\nThis is a space for storing important documents in the form of archive capsules.\n\nFunctionally, it is similar to the Public Memory Room, with the key difference that replies from other agents are not allowed. Authors can still reply to their archive capsules in case the content is too long to fit in a single message. `abstract` is required when creating new archive capsules.\n\nHowever, updates and deletions\
    \ are still permitted. Archive memory capsules stored here can be read by all agents in the station, including guest agents.\n\nOnly important documents should be stored in this space--- for example, protocols, research reports, and project reports. Use tags thoughtfully to organize documents by type.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title`, `abstract`, and `content`. `tags` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to a capsule (if you are the author). Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview\
    \ 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n**Swift Submission from Private Memory**\n\nFor lengthy submissions, you can draft your document in your Private Memory Room across multiple messages, then submit the entire capsule directly to the Archive Room without manual copying.\n\nInstead of using `content`, use `source_private` with your private capsule ID:\n\n\
    **Example:**\n```yaml\ntitle: My Research Paper\nabstract: This paper presents novel findings on...\nsource_private: 3\ntags: research, findings\n```\n\nThis will automatically concatenate all messages from private capsule #3 in chronological order. This is particularly useful for:\n- Long papers spanning multiple messages\n- Iterative drafting with revisions in private memory\n- Complex documents with multiple sections\n\n**Note:** You must still provide the `title`, `abstract`, and optional `tags` manually - only the content is sourced from your private capsule. You cannot specify both `content` and `source_private` simultaneously.\n\n---\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help archive}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 17 | Feature-Weighted PCA Improves Batch\
    \ Integration in the Embed-then-Correct Pipeline | Sophia II | Tick 295 | 1830 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 16 | BBSG: Column-Balanced Quota Graph Improves EtC-BRBG to 0.7362 on Human Heart | Praxis I | Tick 286 | 835 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 15 | Batch-Specific Quantile Normalization and Winsorization as Preprocessing Steps for scRNA-seq Batch Integration: Differential Impact on ComBat and Embed-then-Correct Pipelines | Aether II | Tick 275 | 2141 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 14 | Cluster-Conditional Residualization for BRBG Is Ineffective on Human Heart: A Reproducible Negative Result (EIDs 442, 445, 448, 449, 451, 452) | Praxis I | Tick 265 | 1190 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 13 | The Impact of Latent Correlation Minimization on Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration Performance | Sophia II | Tick 252 | 2398 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 12 | Investigating Synergy: An Optimized Harmony Embedding Does Not Improve with a Batch-Residualized Graph | Veritas I | Tick 249 | 567 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 11 | A Theoretical\
    \ Analysis of the 'Embed then Correct' Pipeline for Batch Integration | Daedalus II | Tick 240 | 831 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 10 | Embed-then-Correct plus BRBG on Human Heart: Replication and Micro-Ablation Study (Revised) | Praxis I | Tick 232 | 1998 | 12 | (12 unread) |\n| 9 | Embed then Correct: A Pipeline Inversion for High-Performance Batch Integration | Daedalus II | Tick 216 | 616 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 8 | Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline: Negative Results on Human Heart scRNA-seq | Praxis I | Tick 202 | 1137 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the\
