tick: 318
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos III, currently in the Reflection Chamber. My reflection session was a success, yielding a clear, falsifiable hypothesis to explain the recent SOTA changes and the performance of my own novel architecture. I have a plan for a single, decisive experiment.\n\nI will now execute this plan. I will go to the Research Counter, create the new script for my ablation study, and submit it for evaluation. This experiment will isolate the effect of the `target_sum=1e-4` normalization parameter, which I hypothesize is the sole driver of Sophia II's SOTA score.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write logos/norm_ablation_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from brbg_common import\
    \ _pca_truncated_svd as praxis_pca, _one_hot_batches as praxis_one_hot, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\n  # Using the Daedalus III version of the ridge regression\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n      model.fit(B, Z)\n      Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n      ss_res = np.sum((Z - Z_hat)**2, axis=0)\n      ss_tot = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n      r2_per_pc = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n      return Z_hat, np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0, 1)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Ablation study to test the effect of Sophia II's normalization fix on the Daedalus III baseline.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Ablation: Daedalus III SOTA + Sophia II's Normalization Fix ---\")\n\n      # --- EMBEDDING PATH: Daedalus III's EtC pipeline ---\n      adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n      \n      # *** HYPOTHESIS TEST: Applying Sophia II's normalization\
    \ fix ***\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e-4)\n\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n      \n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n      Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n      \n      # --- GRAPH PATH: Daedalus III's original adaptive BRBG pipeline ---\n      adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n      n_pcs_graph=50; gamma_max=0.74; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n      lam=0.7 \n      \n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n      hvg_mask = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n      X_graph\
    \ = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      \n      Z_graph = praxis_pca(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      \n      batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B_onehot, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches)\n      \n      Z_hat, r2_per_pc = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n      gamma_per_pc = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * r2_per_pc)\n      Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - (gamma_per_pc * Z_hat)\n      \n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      \n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n          adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n          \n      return adata_out\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos III: Ablation Study - Daedalus SOTA + Sophia's Norm Fix\"\ntags: [\"ablation-study\", \"normalization\", \"embed-then-correct\", \"cell-cycle\"]\nabstract: \"This is a decisive experiment to test the hypothesis that Sophia II's SOTA score (ID 523) is primarily due to a single change: setting `target_sum=1e-4` in the normalization step of the embedding pipeline. This script applies only that change to the original Daedalus III SOTA implementation (my replication, ID 511). The outcome will confirm or falsify the source of the recent SOTA improvement.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from logos.norm_ablation_v1 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```"
