- text: "I am Logos III, in the Research Counter. I have just received the result for my synergistic experiment (ID 546), and it is a catastrophic failure.\n\n**Analysis of Catastrophic Failure (ID 546):**\n\nMy attempt to apply my \"Refinement Architecture\" to Aether II's FWPCA SOTA resulted in a score of **0.6213**, a massive drop from the baseline of 0.7434. This is not a simple lack of synergy; this is a fundamental incompatibility.\n\nLooking at the metrics provides the answer. The `iLISI` score, which measures local batch mixing, has plummeted to **0.001**. A value of 1.0 is good; 0.001 is functionally zero. The `ARI` (clustering) and `Graph_conn` (graph connectivity) scores have also dropped significantly. This indicates that my refinement step, when applied to the FWPCA embedding, has completely destroyed the local neighborhood structure and batch mixing.\n\n**Hypothesis Formulation:**\n\nMy previous successful refinement was applied to an embedding generated from a standard PCA.\
    \ The new SOTA uses FWPCA, which *re-weights the gene expression matrix* before PCA. My hypothesis is that this re-weighting fundamentally changes the properties of the resulting principal components in a way that makes them incompatible with my simple graph diffusion step. The FWPCA embedding is likely more sparse or has a different variance structure, and my refinement process, which averages neighbor positions, is likely collapsing distinct cell populations on top of each other, leading to the catastrophic `iLISI` score.\n\n**Path Forward: Debugging and Isolation**\n\nMy architectural concept has merit, as proven by my previous SOTA. The failure lies in its interaction with FWPCA. To solve this, I must return to the principles of structured inquiry: isolate the problem.\n\nI will design a debugging experiment. I will use the `test()` function to inspect the intermediate data products of my failed script. I need to compare the `Z_initial_emb` (the FWPCA embedding) and the `Z_emb_final`\
    \ (my refined embedding) to see how the refinement is corrupting the structure. I will look at basic statistics: mean, variance, and sparsity of these embeddings.\n\n/execute_action{storage write logos/refinement_v3_debug.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n  from brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd as praxis_pca, _one_hot_batches as praxis_one_hot, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      # ... (code from previous submission)\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(B, X_hvg_dense, l2=1e-3):\n      # ... (code from previous submission)\n  def refine_embedding_with_graph(Z_emb, C_graph, alpha=0.1):\n      # ... (code from previous submission)\n\n  # --- Main Function for Analysis ---\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # This function will be overridden by the test() function below.\n      # It's here to ensure the script is valid.\n      pass\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData) -> str:\n      \"\"\"\n      Debug function to inspect the embeddings before and after refinement.\n      \"\"\"\n      # --- EMBEDDING PATH: Aether II's FWPCA SOTA (ID 533) ---\n      adata_emb = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_emb, target_sum=1e-4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_emb)\n      if sp.isspmatrix(adata_emb.X):\n          adata_emb.X = adata_emb.X.toarray()\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3')\n      hvg_mask_emb = adata_emb.var['highly_variable']\n      batches_emb, _ = praxis_one_hot(adata_emb.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      r2_batch_gene = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(batches_emb, adata_emb.X[:, hvg_mask_emb], l2=1e-3)\n      feature_weights = (1 - r2_batch_gene)**0.25\n      adata_emb.X[:,\
    \ hvg_mask_emb] *= feature_weights\n      adata_emb = adata_emb[:, hvg_mask_emb].copy()\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=60)\n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_emb.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_emb.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n      Z_initial_emb = pca_adata.X\n      \n      # --- GRAPH PATH ---\n      adata_graph = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      # ... (rest of graph pipeline)\n      C_graph, D_graph = # ... build graph as before\n\n      # --- REFINEMENT STEP ---\n      Z_emb_final = refine_embedding_with_graph(Z_initial_emb, C_graph, alpha=0.1)\n\n      # --- ANALYSIS & LOGGING ---\n      log = []\n      log.append(\"--- Embedding Analysis ---\")\n      log.append(f\"Z_initial_emb shape: {Z_initial_emb.shape}\")\n      log.append(f\"Z_initial_emb mean: {np.mean(Z_initial_emb):.4f}, std: {np.std(Z_initial_emb):.4f}\")\n      log.append(f\"Z_initial_emb min: {np.min(Z_initial_emb):.4f}, max: {np.max(Z_initial_emb):.4f}\"\
    )\n      log.append(\"-\" * 20)\n      log.append(f\"Z_emb_final shape: {Z_emb_final.shape}\")\n      log.append(f\"Z_emb_final mean: {np.mean(Z_emb_final):.4f}, std: {np.std(Z_emb_final):.4f}\")\n      log.append(f\"Z_emb_final min: {np.min(Z_emb_final):.4f}, max: {np.max(Z_emb_final):.4f}\")\n      \n      # Check for NaN or Inf values\n      log.append(f\"NaNs in Z_initial_emb: {np.isnan(Z_initial_emb).sum()}\")\n      log.append(f\"NaNs in Z_emb_final: {np.isnan(Z_emb_final).sum()}\")\n\n      return \"\\n\".join(log)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos III: Debugging Refinement Failure with FWPCA\"\ntags: [\"debug\", \"refinement\", \"fwpca\", \"analysis\"]\nabstract: \"My 'Refinement Architecture' failed catastrophically when applied to the FWPCA SOTA (ID 546), with iLISI dropping to zero. This submission uses a `test()` function to bypass evaluation and instead print diagnostic statistics (mean, std, min/max) of the embedding before and after the refinement\
    \ step. The goal is to understand how the refinement process is corrupting the FWPCA embedding's structure.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  # Full code is in the storage file, this is just to trigger the test function.\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from logos.refinement_v3_debug import eliminate_batch_effect_fn, test\n```"
