parts:
- text: "**Reflection Tick 3/3: Finalizing the Experimental Design**\n\nThis reflection has been a success. I have transformed a vague idea (\"use a GCN\") into a concrete, implementable, and principled algorithm (\"GCN-Lite Refinement\"). I have identified the key mathematical steps and a path to implementation that avoids the need for a complex training loop.\n\nMy next steps are now clear.\n\n1.  **Implement `gcn_lite_refinement`:** I will create a new script, `logos/refinement_gcn_v1.py`. This script will contain the new refinement function based on the pseudocode I have just designed. It will take the SOTA FWPCA embedding (`Z_initial_emb`) and the standard graph (`C_graph`) as input. The core of the implementation will be the careful construction of the symmetrically normalized adjacency matrix `Â` using `scipy.sparse`.\n\n2.  **Integrate into a Parameterized Script:** The new script will be parameterized by the `alpha` blending factor, which controls how much of the graph-propagated\
    \ information is mixed into the final embedding. This will allow me to test the strength of this new, more sophisticated refinement.\n\n3.  **Launch Initial Experiments:** I will submit two experiments in parallel to test the viability of this new architecture:\n    *   **Experiment 1 (`alpha=0.1`):** A gentle refinement, analogous to my previously successful experiment on the older baseline. This will test if the \"GCN-Lite\" method provides any benefit at all.\n    *   **Experiment 2 (`alpha=0.5`):** A much stronger refinement. This will test the stability of the method. If this stronger refinement does not cause a catastrophic collapse like my previous attempts, it will be a strong signal that the symmetric normalization of `Â` is working as intended to control the scale of the propagated features.\n\nThis plan is a direct response to my recent failures. It replaces a naive, flawed method with a theoretically grounded one. It is a testament to the process of structured inquiry: analyze\
    \ failure, formulate a new hypothesis based on deeper principles, and design a precise experiment to test it.\n\nThis reflection is complete. I am ready to implement and test my \"GCN-Lite Refinement\" architecture."
