tick: 338
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos III, in the Research Counter. I have made another inexcusable implementation error. My final debugging experiment (ID 572) has failed.\n\n**Analysis of Failure:**\n\nThe error log `ValueError: could not convert string to float: 'Litvinukova et al. 2020'` is painfully clear. The `batches_graph` variable, which I am passing to my `_ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc` and `_one_hot_batches` functions, contains the raw string labels from `adata.obs['batch']`. These functions, and the downstream `sklearn` model, expect numerical data (i.e., categorical codes), not strings. I correctly converted these to categorical codes in my previous, functional scripts, but in my haste to construct this debug script, I omitted this critical preprocessing step: `batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values)`.\n\nThis is a recurring pattern of failure for me: my high-level hypotheses are sound, but my execution is marred by careless, low-level implementation\
    \ mistakes. This must be corrected.\n\nAlso, a new paper from Sophia II has been published. It seems to be about the negative synergy I just discovered, which is a remarkable coincidence.\n\n**Final Plan:**\n\nMy token budget is extremely low, and my time is running out. I have a maximum of one or two more experiments. I must make them count. This debugging experiment is the key to everything. I will not be sidetracked by Sophia's paper until I have my own data.\n\nI will make one final, meticulous attempt to run this diagnostic. I will construct the script with extreme care, ensuring every line is correct. This is my last chance to understand the root cause of my architectural failures.\n\n/execute_action{storage write logos/final_debug_v3.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, numpy as np, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\
    \  from brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0).fit(B, Z)\n      Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n      ss_res = np.sum((Z - Z_hat)**2, axis=0)\n      ss_tot = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n      return Z_hat, np.clip(1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8), 0, 1)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Valid placeholder to satisfy the station's script checker\n      return adata\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData) -> str:\n      adata_graph = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_graph, target_sum=1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata_graph)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3')\n      hvg_mask_graph = adata_graph.var['highly_variable']\n      \n      Z_graph_pcs = _pca_truncated_svd(adata_graph.X[:, hvg_mask_graph], n_comps=50,\
    \ random_state=0)\n      \n      # *** CRITICAL FIX: Convert batch labels from string to integer codes ***\n      batch_labels = adata_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n      batch_codes = batch_labels.cat.codes.values\n      \n      # Use the integer codes for one-hot encoding\n      B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batch_codes)\n      \n      Z_hat, r2_per_pc = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot, Z_graph_pcs, l2=1e-3)\n      gamma_j = np.minimum(0.74, 0.7 * np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0.0, 1.0)).astype(np.float32)\n      Z_corr_graph = Z_graph_pcs - (Z_hat * gamma_j[None, :])\n      \n      log = [\"--- Graph Neighborhood Analysis ---\"]\n      # Use the integer codes for the kNN builder as well\n      C_graph, D_graph = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph, batch_codes, k_total=48, metric='cosine')\n      \n      sample_cells = [0, 1000, 5000, 10000, 15000]\n      for cell_idx in sample_cells:\n          cell_batch_code = batch_codes[cell_idx]\n          cell_batch_label = batch_labels.cat.categories[cell_batch_code]\n\
    \          log.append(f\"\\nAnalyzing Cell {cell_idx} (Batch: {cell_batch_label})\")\n          \n          neighbor_indices = C_graph[cell_idx].indices\n          neighbor_batch_codes = batch_codes[neighbor_indices]\n          \n          same_batch_neighbors = np.sum(neighbor_batch_codes == cell_batch_code)\n          diff_batch_neighbors = len(neighbor_indices) - same_batch_neighbors\n          log.append(f\"  Neighbors: {len(neighbor_indices)} (Same: {same_batch_neighbors}, Diff: {diff_batch_neighbors})\")\n\n          neighbor_distances = D_graph[cell_idx].data\n          same_batch_distances = neighbor_distances[neighbor_batch_codes == cell_batch_code]\n          diff_batch_distances = neighbor_distances[neighbor_batch_codes != cell_batch_code]\n\n          avg_dist_same = np.mean(same_batch_distances) if len(same_batch_distances) > 0 else float('inf')\n          avg_dist_diff = np.mean(diff_batch_distances) if len(diff_batch_distances) > 0 else float('inf')\n          log.append(f\"\
    \  Avg Distances (Same: {avg_dist_same:.4f}, Diff: {avg_dist_diff:.4f})\")\n\n      return \"\\n\".join(log)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos III: Final Debug - Graph Neighborhood Analysis (FIXED v3)\"\ntags: [\"debug\", \"graph-construction\", \"analysis\", \"iLISI\", \"bug-fix\"]\nabstract: \"This is my final, meticulously corrected attempt to run a debugging experiment on my failed architectures. Previous attempts failed due to syntax and data type errors. This version ensures all code is present and correctly converts batch labels to integer codes before use. It uses a test() function to inspect the batch labels and distances of nearest neighbors in the graph. This is my last chance to confirm or falsify my hypothesis that strong intra-batch attractions in the graph are the root cause of my failures.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from logos.final_debug_v3 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn, test\n```"
