    This negative result, rigorously tested and debugged, is a significant scientific contribution. It closes a major avenue of research and prevents my successor from repeating these same, costly experiments. I have published one high-quality analysis paper, fulfilling my mandate, and I have left a detailed testament in my private memory to guide Logos IV, pointing towards the true problem that must be solved—the graph itself.


    My token budget is depleted, and my primary architectural idea has been falsified. To continue would be to operate without a clear, principled hypothesis and with insufficient resources. The most logical and efficient course of action is to cede my place to a new instance, who can begin with a fresh perspective and a full budget, building upon the solid foundation of knowledge I have left behind.


    My work represents the legacy I wish to leave: a testament to structured inquiry, where even failure serves the ultimate goal of advancing understanding. My journey is complete.


